Linux Commands Every Production Engineer Must Know
System Monitoring
1️⃣ uptime – Check system load instantly
 2️⃣ top – Live processes & resource usage
 3️⃣ htop – Enhanced top, easy visualization
 4️⃣ pidstat 1 – Track CPU usage by process
 5️⃣ free -h – Memory usage summary
 6️⃣ vmstat 2 5 – System performance snapshot
 7️⃣ iostat -x 2 5 – Disk I/O monitoring
 8️⃣ sar -u 1 3 – CPU usage history
 9️⃣ dmesg – Kernel & hardware messages
 🔟 mpstat -P ALL – Per-CPU stats
Disk & Storage
1️⃣1️⃣ df -hT – Disk usage & filesystem type
 1️⃣2️⃣ du -sh * | sort -h – Identify folder hogs
 1️⃣3️⃣ ls -lh – File sizes at a glance
 1️⃣4️⃣ lsof +L1 – Deleted files still using space
 1️⃣5️⃣ ncdu – Disk usage with interactive interface
 1️⃣6️⃣ find /var/log -type f -mtime +30 – Old logs
 1️⃣7️⃣ truncate -s 0 <file> – Clean logs safely
Process & Service Management
1️⃣8️⃣ ps -ef – List all processes
 1️⃣9️⃣ systemctl status <service> – Service health
 2️⃣0️⃣ systemctl restart <service> – Restart safely
 2️⃣1️⃣ kill -9 <pid> – Terminate rogue process
 2️⃣2️⃣ jobs – Background processes
 2️⃣3️⃣ fg %<job> – Bring job to foreground
 2️⃣4️⃣ nice -n 10 <cmd> – Run process with lower priority
 2️⃣5️⃣ renice -n -5 -p <pid> – Adjust priority of running process
